- lem-a-sequence-in-a-hausdorff-space-has-at-most-one-limit A1: $X$ is Hausdorff: distinct points have disjoint open neighbourhoods ([[def-hausdorff-space]]).
- thm-a-compact-hausdorff-space-is-regular-and-normal L2: In a Hausdorff space, a point and a disjoint compact set have disjoint open neighbourhoods, and two disjoint compact sets have disjoint open neighbourhoods ([[thm-compact-subset-of-a-hausdorff-space-is-closed]], [[def-hausdorff-space]], [[def-compact-space]]).
