59:**Given:** Topological spaces $X$, $Y$, $Z$; functions $f : X \to Y$ and $g : Y \to Z$; a family $\{\, U_i : i \in I \,\}$ of open subsets of $X$ covering $X$; a natural $n \ge 1$ and closed subsets $F_1, \dots, F_n$ of $X$ covering $X$. For $S \subseteq X$ and $W \subseteq Y$ one has $(f|_S)^{-1}[W] = f^{-1}[W] \cap S$, and $(g \circ f)^{-1}[W'] = f^{-1}[g^{-1}[W']]$ for $W' \subseteq Z$.
