91:**Why this lemma exists, and why it is a lemma.** Three results of this page —
106:**Clause 5 closes a second seam.** The phrase *compact subset of $\mathbb{R}$*
114:**Given:** A set $A \subseteq \mathbb{R}$ with the subspace metric $d_A(x,y) = |x-y|$, a function $f : A \to \mathbb{R}$, and a set $K \subseteq \mathbb{R}$ with the subspace metric $d_K$.
