### thm-homotopy-equivalence-is-an-equivalence-relation
42:1.1 The identity $\operatorname{id}_X:X\to X$ is a homotopy equivalence with itself as homotopy inverse, since both composites equal, and hence are homotopic to, $\operatorname{id}_X$. [A1, L2]
44:1.2 If $f:X\to Y$ has homotopy inverse $g:Y\to X$, the same two homotopies show that $g$ has homotopy inverse $f$. Thus the relation is symmetric. [A1]
