items/lem-a-locally-compact-hausdorff-space-has-a-base-of-open-sets-with-compact-closure.md:92:1.1 By [A1] fix a compact $K \subseteq X$ and an open $O \subseteq X$ with $x \in O \subseteq K$; then $O \subseteq \operatorname{int}(K)$ by [A3], so $x \in \operatorname{int}(K)$. [A1, A3, choose]
