+ ("cor-punctured-rn-homotopy-equivalent-to-the-sphere","ai-altered","ai-generated","semantic-source",[STONYBROOK],"The Stony Brook notes state the deformation retract; the item records its immediate homotopy-equivalence consequence as a separate corollary."),
+ ("fs-a-retract-must-be-a-deformation-retract","ai-altered","ai-generated","semantic-source",[AT],"Hatcher explicitly says not every retraction is a deformation retraction: every space retracts onto a point, whereas deformation retraction to a point forces path-connectedness. The item chooses the two-point discrete specialization."),
+ ("fs-homotopy-equivalent-spaces-are-homeomorphic","ai-altered","ai-generated","semantic-source",[AT],"Hatcher introduces homotopy equivalence as strictly broader than homeomorphism and supplies nonhomeomorphic examples. The item uses the elementary point-versus-real-line specialization."),
+ ("ex-straight-line-homotopy-between-maps-into-rn","ai-altered","ai-generated","semantic-source",[UCR_HOMOTOPY],"This is the convex-target straight-line theorem specialized to the full Euclidean codomain."),
